---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Legal title="Terms of Service" description="The rules for using the Larrikin Coffee Collective ordering app and buying group.">
  <p>
    These terms cover the {site.name} ("we", "us") ordering app and the group buying that runs
    through it. By signing in or placing an order you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>
    We collect members' orders, combine them into a single wholesale order, and arrange pickup
    through local hubs. We are not the roaster and we do not roast or pack the coffee.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Keep your details (name, phone and pickup hub) accurate, and don't let anyone else place
    orders as you. We may remove accounts that misuse the group.
  </p>

  <h2>Orders</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We open and close each order. Any close time shown is a guide only, and we may close, delay or cancel an order.</li>
    <li>Prices and availability come from the supplier's catalogue and can change. If an item becomes unavailable it is removed from your order.</li>
    <li>Once an order has been submitted to the supplier it can't be changed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Payment works on an honour system. After an order closes we email you your total. You pay
    us by bank transfer or cash, then confirm using the link in the email. You agree to pay for
    everything you order. Any membership or service fee is shown in the app before you commit.
  </p>

  <h2>Pickup</h2>
  <p>Orders are collected from your chosen hub.</p>

  <h2>Your consumer rights</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits any rights you have under the Australian Consumer Law that
    can't be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The date above shows when they last changed.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia.</p>

  {site.contactEmail && (
    <>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    </>
  )}
</Legal>
